{"entryId":"1679","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1679:1","sourceSha256":"90fdc503e5027a03003845119b2d5819673bf2227d242b4d15ee5dee14ea47a3","englishSha256":"32fbe04eb282983ae85ffd74567533dbdeb3fa359904193ef2825a9d99f19ee7","citations":[{"id":"1679:1:citation-01","he":[0,61],"en":[76,100],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bamidbar_Rabbah_12.3"},"reference":"Bamidbar Rabbah 12:3","assessment":"Naso names Yehudah son of Rabbi Shmuel and relates that he saw, did not fall, and died. Preserve Heilprin’s bare name.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bamidbar Rabbah 12:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bamidbar_Rabbah_12.3"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]},{"id":"1679:1:citation-02","he":[63,82],"en":[102,137],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eikhah_Rabbah_1.29"},"reference":"Eikhah Rabbah 1:29","assessment":"The parallel relates that the pious man fell and died. Some call him Yehudah Berabbi. It separately says Shmuel saw and did not fall.","evidence":[{"reference":"Eikhah Rabbah 1:29","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eikhah_Rabbah_1.29"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"Keep the bare heading and the diverging Naso and Eikhah accounts.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Bamidbar Rabbah 12:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bamidbar_Rabbah_12.3"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"},{"reference":"Eikhah Rabbah 1:29","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eikhah_Rabbah_1.29"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
